  "limitations": [
    "Small diagnostic sample: repeated-switch medians use three observations per page. These are not percentile SLOs or a load test.",
    "Local is a development server with existing uncommitted changes; production is a separate optimized deployment. The end-to-end measurement methods also differ. Do not use the table as an exact local/production speed ratio.",
    "The database timing phases include request round trips, pagination, deserialization and helper work; they do not isolate PostgreSQL execution time.",
    "selected_phases_ms retains the significant phase measurements; small preparation/scope/extra-data/presentation phases are omitted. The selected phases therefore need not sum exactly to server_ms.",
    "spans_ms are concurrent measurements inside the phases, not additional time to add to server_ms.",
    "jsx_build measures JSX construction only. response_to_commit_ms measures the residual from completed response to browser effect and includes client scheduling. Pure React server/client render CPU was not separately profiled.",
    "Completed resource counts can omit in-flight or prefetched requests. Every measured local navigation had a fresh page sample; repeated navigation did not reuse the previous computed report.",
    "Auth claims/profile/permission subphase logging and layout badge timings were added, but the existing local server stdout was not retrievable in this session. These subphase values are not part of this baseline.",
    "Detailed local diagnostics were not deployed. Production database/calculation/render phase breakdowns, and Dashboard/Orders server totals, remain unavailable.",
    "The production Overview reload took 4161 ms, with 1687.3 ms in the existing report timer including 628.4 ms authentication. The remaining delay was not isolated; it is not proof of a cold start."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "finding": "Recent Order GPM fetches lifetime orders and related line items before selecting ten displayed orders.",
      "evidence": "527 orders, 717 items and 381 production runs loaded per local sample. Repeated commerce spans 1654.2–1665.2 ms.",
      "next_step": "Select the ten eligible orders before loading their items, while preserving existing date/status/scope and costing semantics. Check report totals against the baseline."
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "finding": "Reports await rep settings and profiles sequentially before main data fetching, and repeat the work on tab switches.",
      "evidence": "Two rep lookup phases generally add about 0.5–0.6 seconds locally; one repeat spent 1449.3 ms. Overview/Centers commerce fetching adds roughly 1.1–1.2 seconds on repeated switches.",
      "next_step": "Remove unnecessary metadata dependencies, parallelize independent reads, and evaluate scoped reuse/invalidation for shared report data. Preserve user permissions and freshness."
    },
    {
      "priority": 3,
      "finding": "Dashboard awaits payroll status before its main dashboard queries.",
      "evidence": "Payroll status cost 351.3–854.3 ms across local samples; repeated median 361.6 ms.",
      "next_step": "Run independent payroll and dashboard reads concurrently or load the payroll status separately, then repeat the benchmark."
    },
    {
      "priority": 4,
      "finding": "Calculations and post-response browser work are small relative to fetching in the measured local workflows.",
      "evidence": "Report calculation phases were 2.4–9.2 ms. Repeated response-to-commit residuals across all pages were 8.7–25.9 ms. Middleware auth measured 1.2–3.7 ms.",
      "next_step": "Prioritize fetch volume and serial dependencies before changes to rendering."
    },
    {
      "priority": 5,
      "finding": "Authentication contributes latency and occasional spikes but does not explain most routine report-switch time.",
      "evidence": "Local authentication 115.7–502.5 ms. Production auth_context 36–139.9 ms except the 628.4 ms Overview reload.",
      "next_step": "Use new claims/profile/permission timings in a later comparable server run to determine the source of auth spikes."
    }
  ],
